        "variation": "statement (p1) - rhythmic diminution of the answer (p2) - transposed and re-harmonised into C major (p3) - augmentation at doubled note values across two patterns (p7/p8) - re-orchestrated onto the triangle in the bridge (triangle p3) - final re-harmonisation under the Neapolitan (p9)"
      },
      "bank": {
        "instruments": ["lead-bright", "lead-round", "harm-soft", "bass", "tri-kick", "kick", "snare", "hat-closed", "crash", "dpcm-kit"],
        "rev": 1
      },
      "percussionGap": 8,
      "notes": "three key centres, three DIFFERENT modulation techniques, one per transition. A minor -> C major at frame 7 by pivot chord (the shared Am, held bare across frames 6/7). C major -> D minor at frame 11 by a bare unison lead-in plus F07, which drops the engine speed to 7 and the readout to 128.6 BPM; b flat (notes 46/58/70) is the only accidental the D minor section adds and it is capped at 3 frames. D minor -> A minor at frame 14 by a whole bar of the dominant, E7, with F06 restoring speed 6. Non-diatonic colours: E7's g sharp (68/56/44) at every return to the tonic, and the Neapolitan B flat major opening the coda at frame 21. ENGINE NOTE, and it is a trap: 3xx is a PERSISTENT CHANNEL MODE in this driver and 300 only freezes it - a further note would still refuse to retrigger - so the bridge's portamento is cancelled with 200 (param 0, which is a documented off value and never consults effect memory), not with 300. Second engine note: a duty MACRO overrides Vxx from the next tick, so every Vxx here is a section-level statement of a timbre the instrument's macro then holds, not per-row automation. Decimal params: F param 7 = speed 7 (below speedSplitPoint 32), F param 6 = speed 6, B param 2 = loop to frame 2, D param 12 = enter the coda 12 rows in (a three-beat pickup, written on the last row of frame 20), 0 param 71 = 047 = major triad, 0 param 74 = 04a = dominant seventh, S param 4 cuts a 6-tick row after 4 ticks, G param 2 = a two-tick flam, A param 15 = A0f = a fast swell UP (the y digit slides up - the direction is inverted here), A param 0 cancels it."
    }
  }
